{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 0, "result": {"protocolVersion": "2025-06-18", "capabilities": {"tools": {"listChanged": false}, "resources": {}, "prompts": {}}, "serverInfo": {"name": "ucas", "title": "ucas, a computer algebra system for programmers", "version": "1"}, "instructions": "ucas analyses functions (exhaustively on machine types), does exact algebra and calculus, transforms, number theory and finite fields, and finds cheaper implementations, each answer checked or proved.  Expressions are ucas syntax strings; give parameters types (x: u8, x: f32, x: real) where it matters.  Definitions persist across calls.  An ambiguous input is an error listing its readings: retry with args.assume.KEY.  structuredContent holds the typed result, checks and proof."}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 81, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "the system\n  x = 2 mod 3: x = 2\n    x = 2 (mod 3)\n  x = 3 mod 5: x = 3\n    x = 3 (mod 5)\nx = 8 (mod 15)\n  how: the Chinese remainder theorem, pairwise (moduli that share factors must agree mod their gcd)\n  check: the solution substituted into every congruence: it holds; brute force over 0..14: 1 solution\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 81, "ok": true, "cmd": "crt", "ucas": "crt x = 2 mod 3, x = 3 mod 5", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "crt", "solutions": ["8"], "modulus": "15", "x": ["2 mod 3: x = 2", "2 (mod 3)", "3 mod 5: x = 3", "3 (mod 5)"], "method": "the Chinese remainder theorem, pairwise (moduli that share factors must agree mod their gcd)", "headline": "the system", "more": ["x = 8 (mod 15)"]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "the solution substituted into every congruence: it holds; brute force over 0..14: 1 solution"}], "files": [], "text": "the system\n  x = 2 mod 3: x = 2\n    x = 2 (mod 3)\n  x = 3 mod 5: x = 3\n    x = 3 (mod 5)\nx = 8 (mod 15)\n  how: the Chinese remainder theorem, pairwise (moduli that share factors must agree mod their gcd)\n  check: the solution substituted into every congruence: it holds; brute force over 0..14: 1 solution\n"}, "isError": false}}
